docs {
  # Create Settlement

  - **Method** `POST`
  - **Endpoint** `/api/v1/groups/:groupID/settlements`
  - **Auth** Bearer access token

  ## Description

  Records a payment that already happened outside the app. The caller becomes the sender. Pick a different member of this group with an active account and active membership. The new record starts as `PENDING`. Only a recipient confirmation affects the current settlement balance.

  An active account and active membership with no departure timestamp are required. A site admin also needs active membership. Example IDs are illustrative. Use IDs from your own group. Payments can be changed in `ACTIVE` and `SETTLING`. A `CLOSED` group is read-only.

  ## Enum values

  | Field | Values | Meaning |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | `status` | `PENDING`, `SUCCESS`, `REJECT`, `CANCELED` | Uppercase, case-sensitive payment status. |
  | `group status` | `ACTIVE`, `SETTLING`, `CLOSED` | ACTIVE and SETTLING allow payment writes. CLOSED permits reads. |

  ## Request

  ### Headers
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `Authorization` | `string` | Yes | Bearer access token (`Bearer <token>`). |
  | `Content-Type` | `string` | Yes | `application/json`. Keep the body within 1 MiB. |

  ### Path parameters
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `groupID` | `integer` | Yes | Positive signed 64-bit group ID. Bruno variable `settlementGroupId`. |

  ### Query parameters
  This endpoint has no query parameters.

  ### Body
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `to_member_id` | `integer` | Yes | Positive group membership ID from List Active Recipients or the personal settlement plan. |
  | `amount_toman` | `integer` | Yes | Positive whole-toman amount within signed 64-bit range. |
  | `note` | `string \| null` | No | Optional note, up to 2,000 characters. |
  | `paid_at` | `RFC 3339 timestamp \| null` | No | Date the payment happened. Omit or send null to use the current server time. |
  | `attachment_ids` | `integer[] \| null` | No | Up to 100 unique positive IDs. Each must be an unlinked SETTLEMENT_RECEIPT uploaded by the caller and compatible with the group. |

  Upload any receipt first. In the save request use its `data.id`. Each accepted POST registers a new record.

  ```json
  {
    "to_member_id": 32,
    "amount_toman": 200000,
    "note": "Bank transfer",
    "paid_at": "2026-11-20T14:00:00Z",
    "attachment_ids": [
      1301
    ]
  }
  ```

  ## Response

  **`201 Created`**

  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": {
      "id": 701,
      "group_id": 10,
      "from_member_id": 30,
      "to_member_id": 32,
      "from_member": {
        "member_id": 30,
        "user_id": 130,
        "name": "Ali",
        "avatar_url": null
      },
      "to_member": {
        "member_id": 32,
        "user_id": 132,
        "name": "Sara",
        "avatar_url": null
      },
      "amount_toman": 200000,
      "status": "PENDING",
      "note": "Bank transfer",
      "paid_at": "2026-11-20T14:00:00Z",
      "confirmed_at": null,
      "rejected_at": null,
      "canceled_at": null,
      "created_at": "2026-11-20T14:00:00Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-20T14:00:00Z",
      "is_frozen": false,
      "is_external": false,
      "can_confirm": false,
      "can_reject": false,
      "can_delete": true,
      "attachment_ids": [
        1301
      ],
      "attachments": [
        {
          "id": 1301,
          "original_filename": "receipt.pdf",
          "mime_type": "application/pdf",
          "file_size_bytes": 28413,
          "access_url": "https://storage.example.com/signed/receipt.pdf"
        }
      ],
      "warnings": []
    }
  }
  ```

  ### Response fields

  | Field | Type | Meaning |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | `id` | `integer` | Payment ID used in settlementID. |
  | `group_id` | `integer` | Parent group. |
  | `from_member_id` | `integer` | Sender's group membership ID. |
  | `to_member_id` | `integer` | Recipient's group membership ID. |
  | `from_member / to_member` | `object` | Member profiles for displaying both parties. |
  | `amount_toman` | `integer` | Registered whole-toman amount. |
  | `status` | `string` | Current payment status. |
  | `note` | `string \| null` | Optional note provided during registration. |
  | `paid_at` | `RFC 3339 timestamp` | When the sender says the transfer occurred. |
  | `confirmed_at` | `RFC 3339 timestamp \| null` | Server time of confirmation. |
  | `rejected_at` | `RFC 3339 timestamp \| null` | Server time of rejection. |
  | `canceled_at` | `RFC 3339 timestamp \| null` | Server time of cancellation after the recipient departed. |
  | `created_at` | `RFC 3339 timestamp` | When the payment was recorded. |
  | `updated_at` | `RFC 3339 timestamp` | Most recent payment record update. |
  | `is_frozen` | `boolean` | True when the group is CLOSED. |
  | `is_external` | `boolean` | True if either party has inactive membership or a departure timestamp. |
  | `can_confirm / can_reject` | `boolean` | True for the recipient on a writable PENDING payment. |
  | `can_delete` | `boolean` | True for the sender on a writable PENDING payment. |
  | `attachment_ids` | `integer[]` | Private receipt IDs. Empty when none. |
  | `attachments` | `array` | Receipt metadata. Empty when none. |
  | `attachments[].id` | `integer` | Attachment ID. |
  | `attachments[].original_filename` | `string \| null` | Original display filename. |
  | `attachments[].mime_type` | `string \| null` | Stored MIME type. |
  | `attachments[].file_size_bytes` | `integer \| null` | Stored length in bytes. |
  | `attachments[].access_url` | `string \| null` | Signed download URL when available. Refresh the API response for a new URL after expiration. |
  | `warnings` | `array` | Endpoint-specific advisory messages. Empty when none. |
  | `warnings[].code` | `string` | Stable warning code. |
  | `warnings[].message` | `string` | Displayable explanation. |

  ### Fields of `from_member` and `to_member`

  | Field | Type | Meaning |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | `member_id` | `integer` | Membership ID in this group. |
  | `user_id` | `integer` | Global user ID. |
  | `name` | `string` | Display name, or an empty string when unavailable. |
  | `avatar_url` | `string \| null` | Signed avatar URL when available. |

  Copy `data.id` into `settlementId` for Get, Confirm, Reject or Delete.

  ### Overpayment warning

  If the amount exceeds the sender's current net debt in this group, the record is still created and the following item appears in `warnings`. Net debt is calculated across the group's active memberships.

  ```json
  {
    "code": "PAYMENT_EXCEEDS_CURRENT_DEBT",
    "message": "payment exceeds your current net debt in this group; registration is allowed"
  }
  ```

  ## Errors

  | HTTP | code | error | When it happens |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | 400 | `BAD_REQUEST` | `bad request payload or parameters` | Invalid group ID, malformed/oversize JSON, invalid amount/date/recipient ID, note longer than 2,000 characters, or invalid attachment ID or array length. |
  | 400 | `SETTLEMENT_SELF_PAYMENT` | `you cannot register a payment to yourself` | The recipient is the caller's own membership. |
  | 400 | `SETTLEMENT_DUPLICATE_ATTACHMENTS` | `attachment_ids must not contain duplicate IDs` | The receipt ID list contains duplicates. |
  | 400 | `INVALID_FILE_TYPE` | `file type or format is not supported` | An attachment is not a SETTLEMENT_RECEIPT. |
  | 401 | `MISSING_TOKEN` | `authorization token is missing` | Missing Authorization header or invalid Bearer header format. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_INVALID` | `authorization token is invalid` | Invalid access token, including use of a refresh token in its place. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_EXPIRED` | `authorization token has expired` | Access token expired. Refresh it or sign in again. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_REVOKED` | `authorization token has been revoked` | Access token is blacklisted. |
  | 403 | `USER_INACTIVE` | `user account is deactivated` | Caller account is inactive. |
  | 403 | `SETTLEMENT_FORBIDDEN` | `you do not have permission to access this settlement` | The caller lacks active membership in the group. |
  | 403 | `ATTACHMENT_FORBIDDEN` | `you do not have permission to access or modify this attachment` | Receipt was uploaded by another user, is already linked or is associated with a different group. |
  | 404 | `USER_NOT_FOUND` | `user not found` | Caller account is missing or soft-deleted. |
  | 404 | `GROUP_NOT_FOUND` | `group not found` | Group is missing or soft-deleted. |
  | 404 | `SETTLEMENT_RECIPIENT_NOT_FOUND` | `recipient must be an active member with an active account in this group` | Recipient membership is missing, outside the group or inactive, or the recipient account is missing or inactive. |
  | 404 | `ATTACHMENT_NOT_FOUND` | `attachment not found` | A specified receipt is missing or soft-deleted. |
  | 409 | `SETTLEMENT_GROUP_CLOSED` | `payments cannot be changed after the group is closed` | Payment writes are blocked in CLOSED groups. |
  | 422 | `FINANCIAL_AMOUNT_OUT_OF_RANGE` | `financial balance exceeds the supported range` | The current ledger balance is outside the supported signed 64-bit range. |
  | 500 | `INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR` | `an internal server error occurred` | Database, transaction or token verification dependency failed. |
  | 503 | `STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE` | `storage service is temporarily unavailable` | Required attachment URL signing failed. |

  ### `404 SETTLEMENT_RECIPIENT_NOT_FOUND` example

  ```json
  {
    "success": false,
    "code": "SETTLEMENT_RECIPIENT_NOT_FOUND",
    "error": "recipient must be an active member with an active account in this group"
  }
  ```
}
